  Phase 1.19c4 — FileProvider path mapping for the attachment
  "Save" share-sheet flow.

  Exposes `cacheDir/shared-attachments/` (where
  `ChatScreen.shareDecryptedBytes` writes the decrypted blob
  bytes) as `content://me.lakko.dev.fileprovider/shared/<name>`.
  Other apps that handle the ACTION_SEND chooser (Files, Drive,
  Gmail, Telegram, …) read the content URI with the
  FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION grant that the chooser intent
  carries. The grant is per-Activity-task and expires when the
  receiving app's process is killed — we don't have to
  explicitly revoke.

  Only `cache-path` is exposed. Files dropped into the
  Android cache directory are eligible for OS-level cleanup
  when storage runs low, which matches the "transient share"
  semantic of these blobs perfectly — the user has already
  forwarded the bytes by the time the OS reclaims them.
-->
<paths xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <cache-path
        name="shared"
        path="shared-attachments/" />
</paths>
